/T (HTTP Archive & "No CMS" GrowthData from the HTTP Archive \(which analyzes millions of real mobile/desktop page loads\) shows that the percentage of the web running "No Detectable CMS" rose from ~46.7% to over 48.3%. This confirms that new sites are increasingly built on modern JavaScript/static stacks rather than traditional database-driven CMSs like WordPress)
/E (HTTP Archive & "No CMS" GrowthData from the HTTP Archive \(which analyzes millions of real mobile/desktop page loads\) shows that the percentage of the web running "No Detectable CMS" rose from ~46.7% to over 48.3%. This confirms that new sites are increasingly built on modern JavaScript/static stacks rather than traditional database-driven CMSs like WordPress)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
